# A finality counter only replaces going to a graveyard from the battlefield (CR 122.1h, the ruling): Summon: Esper Maduin
# returned to its owner's hand by Bot2's Boomerang Basics goes there normally, as the card Esper Origins, front face up
# (CR 712.8a: in a hand only the front face's characteristics count), a new object without counters (CR 400.7). Bot2 did
# not control it, so Boomerang Basics draws nothing. On turn 5 Bot1 casts it from hand: it surveils and gains 2, but was
# not cast from a graveyard, so it goes to the graveyard as a sorcery and does not transform.
# Life: 20 + 2 (turn 1) + 2 (flashback, turn 3) + 2 (from hand, turn 5) = 26.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Esper Origins
Forest x3
Forest
Lightning Bolt
Forest
Island
Forest
Swamp
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Boomerang Basics
Island x18

